<Concept title="Combat progression and Photon Blasts" section="States">
<p>One playtest covers #723, #732, #343, #734 and #342. This contract supersedes
older placeholder real-time damage math. Original references and deliberate
remake choices are recorded below; owner balance review remains pending.</p>
<h2>Damage and equipment</h2>
<ul>
<li>Physical hits MUST combine class, mag, material, unit and weapon stats.
Weapon grind and family percentages MUST belong to the equipped instance;
family percentages modify weapon ATP only. Weapon accuracy and hit percentage
MUST reach hit resolution. Normal and strong attacks MUST use distinct power
and accuracy modifiers. Existing combo reach and timing remain in force.</li>
<li>The shared numeric resolver MUST subtract defense from modified attack,
divide by five with integer truncation, clamp negative damage to zero, then
apply resistance and critical modifiers. A critical adds half the integer damage.
The default part multiplier is one. Attack variance remains the current ±10%
remake choice pending full original weapon min/max extraction.</li>
<li>Original evidence: psz-re tools/parttable.py and ARM9 FUN_02042A4C
(the subtraction and division by 5, critical addition, reciprocal body-part
multiplier); FUN_02042964 (accuracy × 4/10 minus evasion × 0x333/4096,
then attack accuracy multiplier). Pure fixtures MUST pin numeric boundaries,
zero damage, attributes, grind caps and the three recovered accuracy samples.</li>
<li>Strong attacks use 1.5× power and 0.7× accuracy as explicit provisional
remake tuning; weapon special payloads fall back to the weapon resource when
an instance has no override. This does not implement the full Photon Arts roster
or claim all existing status payloads match PSZ. Native Heat, Ice and Slow
map explicitly to burn, freeze and slow using existing Godot lifetimes and proc
chances; these mappings are remake interpretations pending the full #724 audit.
Other native specials remain unsupported; no invented life/meseta costs or
instant-kill behavior is added.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Progression and grinding</h2>
<ul>
<li>Enemy level MUST be fixed by authored quest/area and difficulty, never the
current player level. It MUST remain stable on revisits and reload. Level-derived
HP, attack, defense, evasion and EXP MUST be applied to per-spawn data copies;
registry resources MUST NOT be mutated. Target feedback MUST show level.</li>
<li>Area base levels and growth slopes are remake choices. The original uses
three difficulty rows (psz-re data/enemy_stat_table.json, FUN_02035598) and
additional quest/party scalers; these do not establish an original enemy-level
curve. Sixty-five mapped enemies use recovered HP, physical min/max ATP, DFP and EVP
rows before the authored level extension. Existing authored stats remain the
tuning baseline for unmapped enemies. The unread EXP-shaped original column is
not treated as verified EXP.</li>
<li>EXP MUST be awarded once on actual enemy death and remain available in character progression screens.
Level-up MUST preserve material HP/PP bonuses. Negative EXP grants MUST NOT
reduce progression. Save/reload MUST preserve levels, equipment and upgrades.</li>
<li>Grinding MUST validate current ownership, current grind, cap and required material at commit time. Inventory Use applies a Monogrinder (+1), Digrinder (+2) or Trigrinder (+3) to the equipped weapon, clamps to its cap and consumes one item without a meseta fee. Use MUST be disabled for a capped, absent or incompatible weapon. Inventory and equipment MUST show the per-instance grind suffix and upgraded ATP. The Tekker retains its separate +1 service and displayed fee, validating carried meseta at commit time; rejection changes nothing.
Original physical grinding MUST add two ATP per level (psz-re tools/wpnprm.py,
16 anchored handgun/rifle records). Existing rarity requirements and fees are retained
remake values, pending the weapon-economy design. No failure chance is added.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Photon Blasts</h2>
<ul>
<li>The gauge MUST range from zero to 10000 and fill the four separate blocks of the HP/PP HUD rim clockwise in yellow. Its diagonal gaps and black center MUST remain unfilled. Playtest guidance MUST NOT appear beneath the production HUD. It MUST charge from actual damage dealt/taken, excluding misses,
overkill, invulnerability and blast damage itself. An evolved equipped mag
MUST supply the blast; an unevolved mag MUST NOT fire.</li>
<li>Evidence: psz-re nodes/sys.photon-blast-effects.json; FUN_020AE168 gates
10000 and a valid type; FUN_0203A850 clears gauge on mag equip; FUN_020B964C
adds bucketed damage ratios using PB parameter data and requiring mag level above nine. The current
implementation uses the first selector row; the exact selector identity and
caller routing of six versus ten buckets remain unverified. These are explicit
integration assumptions, not claimed original fidelity. Blast types
come from FUN_020A8BB0 and existing mag resources.</li>
<li>Activation MUST consume the gauge once, lock actions during its short
presentation and deliver its effect once. Invalid/dead/interrupted activation
MUST NOT spend the gauge. Scene exit MUST cancel pending delivery safely.
Dedicated B / right-stick-click inputs and the clickable HUD rim provide keyboard/controller and touch access without requiring a palette assignment. Party chains and the original summon rigs remain separate work.</li>
<li>Granir and Pacifal are damaging blasts; Midgul applies attack/defense
weakening; Flozir provides a timed PP benefit. Presentation, radii, durations and
unrecovered potency are explicitly provisional remake values, not inferred
from effect names. Tests MUST cover every supported blast and lifecycle reset.</li>
</ul>
<p>Verification: systems_progression_tests.gd plus systems_progression_probe.tscn
on imported player/enemy rigs, then the existing quest regression matrix.</p>
<p>Owner review: Kion assessed Systems as C on 2026-10-11 after the PR #752 Mac playtest. The Coliseum exit fix has regression coverage; quest/free-roam traversal and remaining fidelity work still need follow-up.</p>
<h2>One combined playtest</h2>
<ol>
<li>Create a fresh Hunter. Fight an ordinary early-area enemy with the starter
Saber; observe landed damage, misses, its level and HP. Compare normal and strong
attacks. The deterministic live fixture currently needs six swings including
misses for a 95-HP level-one Ghowl.</li>
<li>Earn level two through kills and check EXP, HP and stats. Save, quit and
reload. Later areas and higher difficulties should retain their own enemy levels.</li>
<li>At the Tekker, grind a weapon, check the preview and wallet/material count,
then return to combat. Compare a matching family attribute and a neutral target.
A second copy of the same weapon must retain its own grind. Use one of each grinder from inventory on an unground Saber: the result MUST be Saber +6 with 49 weapon ATP.</li>
<li>Feed the Mag to its first evolution. Charge PB in combat, then use the
B key, right-stick click or the charged HUD rim. Check one activation,
its effect and return of control. The four stat paths select the four blast types.</li>
<li>Try an available Heat/Ice/Slow weapon's strong attack. Check visible status
and expiry. Report balance and presentation feedback for the whole build.</li>
</ol>
<p>Automated entry points: <code>res://scripts/tools/systems_progression_probe.tscn</code>
and <code>res://scripts/tools/technique_progression_probe.tscn</code>, with an isolated
XDG_DATA_HOME and PSZ_PROBE_PACK pointing at the asset pack. Run
<code>python3 scripts/tools/check_systems_reference.py /path/to/psz-re</code>
to reproduce the original-data comparison.</p>
<p>Preserved remake choices: class stat curves, EXP rewards, ±10% attack variance,
5% base critical chance, 15% innate-weapon bonus, strong-attack modifiers,
area-level slopes, shop fees and PB effect potency/presentation. Unrecovered
zero-power technique-weapon resources, party chains, complete original status
and PA semantics, and full damage/part-resistance fidelity remain open.</p>
<p>Original <code>FUN_02042964</code> bypasses the physical hit roll for attack kinds 2 and 3; techniques and PB effects likewise bypass weapon accuracy. Zero-ATP technique weapons are excluded from grinding until their original stat mapping is implemented, so the shop cannot charge for an ineffective upgrade.</p>
</Concept>
